      "text": "Adding a 1-qubit error to the 2-qubit `cx` gate raises a `NoiseError`, because the error's qubit count does not match the gate's. The fix is a 2-qubit depolarizing error for `cx`, which samples uniformly from the 15 non-identity two-qubit Paulis. The single-qubit error stays on `u1`/`u2`/`u3` and is applied to each qubit separately.\n\nI also changed the import. `qiskit.providers.aer` was removed in current Qiskit, so the same names now come from `qiskit_aer`. If you are on an older Qiskit where the original import still works, you can keep the original import line.\n\n```python\n# FIX: deprecated/removed module path qiskit.providers.aer -> qiskit_aer, because Aer now lives in the separate qiskit_aer package\nfrom qiskit_aer.noise import NoiseModel, depolarizing_error\n\nnoise_model = NoiseModel()\n\nerror = depolarizing_error(0.05, 1)\nnoise_model.add_all_qubit_quantum_error(error, ['u1', 'u2', 'u3'])\n\n# FIX: 1-qubit error applied to 2-qubit 'cx' -> use a 2-qubit depolarizing_error, because the error's qubit count must match the gate's\nnoise_model.add_all_qubit_quantum_error(depolarizing_error(0.05, 2), ['cx'])\n\nprint(noise_model)\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
